 "notes": "Quantpedia lunch effect, long-only 12:00-14:00 leg (market at the 12:00 open, 0.4% stop, clock exit at the 14:00 open, macro/FOMC days skipped). MNQ fixed defaults: MAIN 364 trades / +6,868 / PF 1.315 / Sharpe 1.17 but 2025-04-09 alone is +3,089 (45% of net; ex that day PF 1.17), PRIOR 304 / +650 / PF 1.045, 2015-2024 1,972 / -4,891 / PF 0.91. MES (the paper's instrument) is negative in every period and every grid cell (MAIN PF 0.96, PRIOR 0.93, 2015-24 0.83). Reversal variant (short 11-12 then long) PF 0.74-0.98 everywhere: the 11:00-12:00 hour is positive on our data. Raw profile: 12:00-14:00 mean 0.0 bp/day on SPX 2010-2024 (-0.2 NDX), sign follows the year's drift; opex midday -4 to -5 bp (t -1.8) is the one consistent slot; mean gross per trade 2015-2024 is +0.7 (MES) / -0.2 (MNQ) vs 3.80 / 2.30 costs. Grid: MNQ 3/16 cells PF>1 on both periods (all long_only/14:00), MES 0/16; all short_then_long cells negative. Walk-forward OOS 2025-01..2026-09 (MNQ): 401 trades, net +4,379, PF 1.185, Sharpe 0.76, 14/21 positive months, maxDD -2,230; 2025-04 is +2,586 (59% of OOS net) and 2025-04-09 alone +3,089 (ex that day net +1,290 / daily PF 1.055; ex April PF 1.08); 2025 PF 1.35 vs 2026 PF 0.997 (net -38), the 2023-24 OOS folds are 7/8 negative (net -1339), whole OOS 2023-26 PF 1.07. Lucid on the OOS stream: 5 micros pass 0.178 / pass-within-21 0.156, P(first payout) 0.008, expected net -118, lower bound -146 = zero-edge control -> not recommended at any size. Verdict marginal by the mechanical rule (WF PF >= 1.03 on >= 40 trades) only; honest reading: a 2025-26 MNQ tape effect concentrated in April 2025, no edge net of costs over 2015-2024, dead on MES. Reusable output: lunch profile by year / macro / opex (lunch_profile_summary.csv).",
